===
# LaTeX Inline Math

Inline equations use dollar signs: $E = mc^2$

The quadratic formula $x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}$ is fundamental.

===
# LaTeX Display Math - Basic

```latex
x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}
```

===
# LaTeX - Integrals

```latex
\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx = F(b) - F(a)
```

===
# LaTeX - Limits

```latex
\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{1}{x} = 0
```

===
# LaTeX - Summation

```latex
\sum_{i=1}^{n} i = \frac{n(n+1)}{2}
```

===
# LaTeX - Product

```latex
\prod_{i=1}^{n} i = n!
```

===
# LaTeX - Matrices

```latex
\begin{pmatrix}
a & b \\
c & d
\end{pmatrix}
\begin{pmatrix}
x \\
y
\end{pmatrix}
=
\begin{pmatrix}
ax + by \\
cx + dy
\end{pmatrix}
```

===
# LaTeX - Greek Letters

```latex
\alpha, \beta, \gamma, \delta, \epsilon, \theta, \lambda, \mu, \pi, \sigma, \omega
```

```latex
\Delta, \Gamma, \Lambda, \Sigma, \Omega
```

===
# LaTeX - Complex Equations

Euler's identity:

```latex
e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0
```

Schrödinger equation:

```latex
i\hbar\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\Psi = \hat{H}\Psi
```

===
# LaTeX - Fractions and Roots

```latex
\frac{1}{\sqrt{2\pi\sigma^2}} e^{-\frac{(x-\mu)^2}{2\sigma^2}}
```
